Build an analytics feature for QuizSnap: $ARGUMENTS

## Pre-Flight (Read First)
1. Read `CLAUDE.md` Section 4 — `AnalyticsEvent` and `QuizResponse` canonical models
2. Read `CLAUDE.md` Section 7 — billing plans (analytics tiers differ by plan)

## Agent Routing

| Analytics Feature        | Primary Agent         | Support Agents                     |
|--------------------------|-----------------------|------------------------------------|
| Event tracking           | `analytics-builder`   | `storefront-builder`               |
| Dashboard UI             | `analytics-builder`   | `admin-builder`, `polaris-design-system` |
| Aggregation queries      | `analytics-builder`   | `prisma-queries`                   |
| Revenue attribution      | `analytics-builder`   | `recommendation-engine`            |
| Funnel analysis          | `analytics-builder`   | `scoring-engine`                   |
| Export / download        | `export-service`      | `analytics-builder`                |
| Per-quiz analytics tab   | `analytics-builder`   | `quiz-builder`                     |

## Canonical: AnalyticsEvent Model

```prisma
model AnalyticsEvent {
  id        String   @id @default(cuid())
  shop      String                           // ALWAYS present — shop scope
  quizId    String
  eventType String
  sessionId String
  data      String   @default("{}")          // JSON: event-specific payload
  revenue   Float    @default(0)
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())

  @@index([shop, quizId, eventType])
  @@index([shop, createdAt])
  @@index([quizId, createdAt])
}
```

## Canonical Event Types

| Event Type          | Trigger                               | data Payload                          |
|---------------------|---------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| `quiz_started`      | User answers first question           | `{ source: "embed|popup", quizId }`   |
| `question_answered` | User answers any question             | `{ questionId, answerId, value }`     |
| `quiz_completed`    | User reaches results page             | `{ resultPageId, score, duration }`   |
| `product_clicked`   | User clicks recommended product       | `{ productGid, resultPageId }`        |
| `added_to_cart`     | User adds product from results        | `{ productGid, variantId }`           |
| `purchase`          | Attribution event after quiz          | `{ orderId, revenue }`                |

> Note: Use these exact event type strings. Not `quiz_start`, not `quiz_complete`.

## Implementation Steps

### Step 1: Event Tracking (Storefront)

Events fire from the widget and POST to the public analytics endpoint:

```typescript
// Widget sends events to public API:
// POST /api/quiz/:slug/submit — for quiz_completed
// POST /api/analytics — for intermediate events (if implemented)

// Server-side event recording:
await db.analyticsEvent.create({
  data: {
    shop,          // NEVER shopId
    quizId,
    eventType,     // Use canonical event types above
    sessionId,
    data: JSON.stringify(payload),
    revenue: 0,
    createdAt: new Date(),
  },
});
```

### Step 2: Aggregation Queries

```typescript
// app/services/analytics.server.ts

// Completion rate
const [starts, completions] = await db.$transaction([
  db.analyticsEvent.count({
    where: { shop, quizId, eventType: "quiz_started", createdAt: { gte: startDate } },
  }),
  db.analyticsEvent.count({
    where: { shop, quizId, eventType: "quiz_completed", createdAt: { gte: startDate } },
  }),
]);
const completionRate = starts > 0 ? (completions / starts) * 100 : 0;

// Question-level drop-off (ALWAYS scope by shop + quizId)
const questionAnswers = await db.analyticsEvent.groupBy({
  by: ["data"],  // parse questionId from data JSON
  where: { shop, quizId, eventType: "question_answered" },
  _count: true,
  orderBy: { _count: { data: "desc" } },
});

// Revenue attribution
const revenue = await db.analyticsEvent.aggregate({
  where: { shop, quizId, eventType: "purchase" },
  _sum: { revenue: true },
});
```

### Step 3: Dashboard UI (Polaris v13)

```tsx
// app/routes/app.quizzes.$id.analytics.tsx
import { useLoaderData, useNavigation } from "react-router";  // NOT @remix-run/react
import { Page, Layout, Card, Text, BlockStack, InlineStack,
         SkeletonBodyText, DataTable, Select } from "@shopify/polaris";

// Metric Card pattern:
<Card>
  <BlockStack gap="200">
    <Text as="h3" variant="headingSm" tone="subdued">Completion Rate</Text>
    <Text as="p" variant="heading2xl" fontWeight="bold">{completionRate}%</Text>
    <Text as="p" variant="bodySm" tone="subdued">
      {completions} of {starts} started
    </Text>
  </BlockStack>
</Card>

// Date range selector:
<Select
  label="Date range"
  options={[
    { label: "Last 7 days", value: "7d" },
    { label: "Last 30 days", value: "30d" },
    { label: "Last 90 days", value: "90d" },
  ]}
  value={dateRange}
  onChange={setDateRange}
/>

// Loading state (Law 9):
const navigation = useNavigation();
if (navigation.state === "loading") {
  return <SkeletonBodyText lines={8} />;
}

// Empty state (Law 10):
if (totalEvents === 0) {
  return (
    <EmptyState
      heading="No analytics data yet"
      image="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0262/4071/2726/files/emptystate-files.png"
    >
      <p>Publish your quiz and share it with customers to start collecting data.</p>
    </EmptyState>
  );
}
```

### Step 4: Key Metrics to Track

```typescript
// KPIs:
const metrics = {
  totalStarts: number,        // quiz_started events
  totalCompletions: number,   // quiz_completed events
  completionRate: number,     // completions / starts * 100
  conversionRate: number,     // added_to_cart / completions * 100
  averageScore: number,       // avg score from QuizResponse
  totalRevenue: number,       // sum of revenue from purchase events
  topResultPage: string,      // most common result page
};
```

### Step 5: Quality Gate

- [ ] All DB queries scoped by `shop` (not `shopId`)
- [ ] All event types use canonical names from table above
- [ ] `authenticate.admin(request)` first in every loader/action
- [ ] Loading state on all data sections
- [ ] Empty state when no events exist
- [ ] `shopify.toast.show()` for any export mutations
- [ ] No Polaris `<Toast>/<Frame>` pattern
- [ ] All imports from `react-router` not `@remix-run/react`

## Output Format

```
## Analytics Feature: [Feature Name]

### Metrics Implemented
- [Metric name]: [calculation method]

### Events
- [Event type]: [trigger and data payload]

### Dashboard Components
- [Component]: [what it shows]

### Files
- [path] — [purpose]

### Quality
- TypeScript: PASS/FAIL
- Shop-scoped queries: PASS/FAIL
- Empty state: HANDLED/MISSING
- Loading state: HANDLED/MISSING
- Event types correct: PASS/FAIL
```

