Build an API endpoint for QuizSnap: $ARGUMENTS

## Pre-Flight (Read First)
1. Read `CLAUDE.md` Law 1 (Auth First), Law 2 (Shop Scoping), Law 5 (CORS)
2. Read `CLAUDE.md` Section 8.2 — Public API route template

## Agent Routing

| API Type                  | Primary Agent       | Support Agents              |
|---------------------------|---------------------|-----------------------------|
| Public storefront API     | `api-builder`       | `storefront-builder`        |
| Admin API action          | `admin-builder`     | `form-validator`            |
| Webhook receiver          | `webhook-handler`   | `security-auditor`          |
| Quiz submission endpoint  | `api-builder`       | `recommendation-engine`     |
| Rate limiting             | `rate-limiter`      | `api-builder`               |

## Route Types

| Route Pattern            | URL                         | Auth Method                      |
|--------------------------|-----------------------------|----------------------------------|
| `app/routes/app.*.tsx`   | `/app/*`                    | `authenticate.admin(request)`    |
| `app/routes/api.*.tsx`   | `/api/*`                    | CORS + optional shop validation  |
| `app/routes/webhooks.*.tsx` | `/webhooks/*`           | `authenticate.webhook(request)`  |

> There is NO `public.*` route prefix. Public routes use `api.*`.

## CORS Headers (Required on ALL `api.*` responses — Law 5)

```typescript
// app/utils/cors.ts
export const CORS_HEADERS = {
  "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": "*",
  "Access-Control-Allow-Methods": "GET, POST, OPTIONS",
  "Access-Control-Allow-Headers": "Content-Type",
} as const;

// ALWAYS handle OPTIONS preflight:
if (request.method === "OPTIONS") {
  return new Response(null, { status: 204, headers: CORS_HEADERS });
}

// ALWAYS include CORS on error responses too:
return json({ error: "Not found" }, { status: 404, headers: CORS_HEADERS });
```

## Implementation Steps

### Step 1: Design the API Contract

Define before building:
- HTTP method (GET for reads, POST for writes)
- Route path (`api.quiz.$slug.tsx`, `api.quiz.$slug.submit.tsx`)
- Request body / query parameters schema (use Zod)
- Response shape with status codes
- Error response format

### Step 2: Implement Admin Route (Protected)

```typescript
// app/routes/app.something.tsx
import { json, type ActionFunctionArgs } from "@shopify/shopify-app-react-router";
import { authenticate } from "~/shopify.server";
import db from "~/db.server";

export async function action({ request }: ActionFunctionArgs) {
  const { session } = await authenticate.admin(request);  // FIRST — always
  const formData = await request.formData();
  const intent = formData.get("intent") as string;
  const shop = session.shop;  // NEVER trust shop from client

  try {
    switch (intent) {
      case "create": {
        // ALWAYS scope with shop
        const result = await db.quiz.create({ data: { shop, title: "..." } });
        return json({ success: true, id: result.id });
      }
      default:
        return json({ error: "Unknown intent" }, { status: 400 });
    }
  } catch (error) {
    return json({ error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : "Error" }, { status: 500 });
  }
}
```

### Step 3: Implement Public API Route

```typescript
// app/routes/api.quiz.$slug.tsx
import { json, type LoaderFunctionArgs } from "react-router";
import db from "~/db.server";
import { CORS_HEADERS } from "~/utils/cors";

export async function loader({ request, params }: LoaderFunctionArgs) {
  if (request.method === "OPTIONS") {
    return new Response(null, { status: 204, headers: CORS_HEADERS });
  }

  const { slug } = params;
  const url = new URL(request.url);
  const shop = url.searchParams.get("shop");

  // Validate shop param (NEVER trust raw input)
  if (!slug || !shop || !/^[a-zA-Z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9\-]*\.myshopify\.com$/.test(shop)) {
    return json({ error: "Invalid request" }, { status: 400, headers: CORS_HEADERS });
  }

  try {
    const quiz = await db.quiz.findUnique({
      where: { shop_slug: { shop, slug } },
      include: {
        questions: {
          include: { answers: { orderBy: { position: "asc" } } },
          orderBy: { position: "asc" },
        },
        resultPages: { orderBy: { position: "asc" } },
      },
    });

    if (!quiz || quiz.status !== "active") {
      return json({ error: "Quiz not found" }, { status: 404, headers: CORS_HEADERS });
    }

    const parseSafe = <T>(str: string, fallback: T): T => {
      try { return JSON.parse(str) as T; } catch { return fallback; }
    };

    return json({
      id: quiz.id,
      title: quiz.title,
      settings: parseSafe(quiz.settings, {}),
      styling: parseSafe(quiz.styling, {}),
      questions: quiz.questions.map((q) => ({
        ...q,
        settings: parseSafe(q.settings, {}),
        logic: parseSafe(q.logic, {}),
        answers: q.answers.map((a) => ({
          ...a,
          productTags: parseSafe(a.productTags, [] as string[]),
        })),
      })),
    }, { headers: CORS_HEADERS });
  } catch (error) {
    return json({ error: "Internal error" }, { status: 500, headers: CORS_HEADERS });
  }
}
```

### Step 4: Implement Webhook Route

```typescript
// app/routes/webhooks.app.uninstalled.tsx
import { authenticate } from "~/shopify.server";
import db from "~/db.server";

export async function action({ request }: ActionFunctionArgs) {
  const { shop, session, topic } = await authenticate.webhook(request);
  // HMAC validation is done by authenticate.webhook — do NOT duplicate

  try {
    // Idempotency: check before deleting
    const existing = await db.subscription.findUnique({ where: { shop } });
    if (existing) {
      await db.subscription.delete({ where: { shop } });
    }
    // Delete shop-specific data (quizzes cascade via onDelete: Cascade)
    await db.quiz.deleteMany({ where: { shop } });
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(`Webhook ${topic} failed:`, error);
  }

  return new Response(null, { status: 200 });
}
```

### Step 5: Input Validation with Zod

```typescript
import { z } from "zod";

const QuizSubmitSchema = z.object({
  sessionId: z.string().min(1),
  answers: z.array(z.object({
    questionId: z.string().cuid(),
    answerId: z.string().cuid().optional(),
    value: z.string().optional(),
  })),
  email: z.string().email().optional(),
});

// In action:
const body = await request.json();
const parsed = QuizSubmitSchema.safeParse(body);
if (!parsed.success) {
  return json({ error: "Invalid input", details: parsed.error.flatten() },
    { status: 400, headers: CORS_HEADERS });
}
```

### Step 6: Quality Gate

- [ ] CORS headers on EVERY response in `api.*` routes (including errors)
- [ ] OPTIONS preflight returns 204
- [ ] Admin routes: `authenticate.admin(request)` FIRST
- [ ] Webhook routes: `authenticate.webhook(request)` — never skip
- [ ] All inputs validated with Zod
- [ ] Shop param validated against regex for public routes
- [ ] No `any` types in response shapes
- [ ] All imports from `react-router` (not `@remix-run/react`)

## Output Format

```
## API Endpoint: [Name]

### Endpoint
- Method: GET/POST/PUT/DELETE
- Path: [route file → URL]
- Type: admin/public/webhook
- Auth: admin session | HMAC | CORS-only

### Request
- Params: [URL parameters]
- Body: [Request body shape with types]
- Headers: [Required headers]

### Response
- 200: [Success shape]
- 400: [Validation error shape]
- 401/403: [Auth error shape]
- 404: [Not found shape]
- 500: [Server error shape]

### Files
- [path] — [purpose]

### Security
- CORS: CONFIGURED/N/A
- Input validation: PASS/FAIL
- Auth check: PASS/FAIL
- Shop scoping: PASS/FAIL
```

