Optimize performance in QuizSnap: $ARGUMENTS

## Pre-Flight (Read First)
1. Read `CLAUDE.md` Section 12 — production performance targets
2. Identify the specific area from $ARGUMENTS before optimizing

## Performance Targets (CLAUDE.md Section 12)

| Area                  | Target                      |
|-----------------------|-----------------------------|
| Admin API responses   | < 200ms p95                 |
| Widget JS bundle      | < 20KB gzipped (hard limit) |
| Widget first paint    | < 100ms on 3G               |
| Prisma queries        | No N+1 (use include + _count)|
| DB index coverage     | All WHERE clauses hit index |

## Agent Routing

| Optimization Area       | Primary Agent           | Support Agents              |
|-------------------------|-------------------------|-----------------------------|
| Database queries / N+1  | `prisma-queries`        | `performance-optimizer`     |
| Page load speed         | `performance-optimizer` | `admin-builder`             |
| Widget performance      | `storefront-builder`    | `responsive-builder`        |
| API response time       | `api-builder`           | `prisma-queries`            |
| Bundle size             | `storefront-builder`    | (build tools)               |
| Parallel loader queries | `admin-builder`         | `prisma-queries`            |

## Database Optimizations

### N+1 Query Detection and Fix

```typescript
// ── RED FLAG: N+1 loop ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
for (const quiz of quizzes) {
  const count = await db.question.count({ where: { quizId: quiz.id } }); // N+1!
  const responses = await db.quizResponse.count({ where: { quizId: quiz.id } }); // N+1!
}

// ── CORRECT: Single query with _count ────────────────────────────────────────
const quizzes = await db.quiz.findMany({
  where: { shop },
  include: {
    _count: { select: { questions: true, responses: true } },
  },
  select: {
    id: true, title: true, status: true, completions: true,
    _count: { select: { questions: true } },
  },
});

// ── RED FLAG: Over-fetching large JSON blobs ──────────────────────────────────
await db.quiz.findMany({ where: { shop } }); // Returns settings + styling blobs

// ── CORRECT: Select only needed fields ───────────────────────────────────────
await db.quiz.findMany({
  where: { shop },
  select: { id: true, title: true, slug: true, status: true, completions: true, updatedAt: true },
  orderBy: { updatedAt: "desc" },
});
```

### Parallel Queries (React Router Loaders)

```typescript
// ── WRONG: Sequential queries (slow) ─────────────────────────────────────────
const quizzes = await db.quiz.findMany({ where: { shop } });
const subscription = await db.subscription.findUnique({ where: { shop } });
const totalResponses = await db.quizResponse.count({ where: { shop } });

// ── CORRECT: Parallel with Promise.all ───────────────────────────────────────
const [quizzes, subscription, totalResponses] = await Promise.all([
  db.quiz.findMany({ where: { shop }, select: { id: true, title: true, status: true } }),
  db.subscription.findUnique({ where: { shop } }),
  db.quizResponse.count({ where: { shop } }),
]);
```

### Database Indexes

All WHERE clauses must hit an index. Verify in `schema.prisma`:

```prisma
model Quiz {
  @@index([shop])            // All quiz queries
  @@index([shop, status])    // Filtered list queries
}

model AnalyticsEvent {
  @@index([shop, quizId, eventType])  // Funnel queries
  @@index([shop, createdAt])          // Date range queries
  @@index([quizId, createdAt])        // Per-quiz analytics
}

model QuizResponse {
  @@index([quizId, shop])      // Response queries
  @@index([shop, createdAt])   // Date range queries
  @@index([email])             // Email lookup
}

model ProductMapping {
  @@index([shop])              // Shop product list
  @@index([shop, status])      // Active products only
}
```

### Pagination for Large Datasets

```typescript
// Cursor-based pagination (more efficient than offset for large datasets)
const [records, total] = await db.$transaction([
  db.quizResponse.findMany({
    where: { shop, quizId },
    take: 20,
    ...(cursor ? { skip: 1, cursor: { id: cursor } } : {}),
    orderBy: { createdAt: "desc" },
  }),
  db.quizResponse.count({ where: { shop, quizId } }),
]);
```

## Page Load Optimizations

### Defer Non-Critical Data (React Router)

```typescript
