Create a quiz template for QuizSnap: $ARGUMENTS

## Pre-Flight (Read First)
1. Read `CLAUDE.md` Section 4 — `QuizTemplate` canonical model
2. Read `CLAUDE.md` Section 4 — `Quiz`, `Question`, `Answer`, `ResultPage` models (template data mirrors this)
3. Templates are stored as JSON in `QuizTemplate.templateData` — parse with try/catch

## Agent Routing

| Template Category     | Primary Agent         | Domain Expert                  |
|-----------------------|-----------------------|--------------------------------|
| Skincare routine      | `template-builder`    | `skincare-quiz-expert`         |
| Fashion / style       | `template-builder`    | `fashion-quiz-expert`          |
| Food / nutrition      | `template-builder`    | `food-quiz-expert`             |
| Fitness / wellness    | `template-builder`    | `fitness-quiz-expert`          |
| Gift finder           | `template-builder`    | `general-quiz-expert`          |
| Home decor            | `template-builder`    | `general-quiz-expert`          |
| Pet products          | `template-builder`    | `general-quiz-expert`          |
| General product match | `template-builder`    | `general-quiz-expert`          |

## Canonical: QuizTemplate Model

```prisma
model QuizTemplate {
  id           String   @id @default(cuid())
  name         String
  description  String?
  category     String   // skincare | fashion | food | tech | fitness | general
  thumbnail    String?
  templateData String   @default("{}")  // JSON: full quiz structure
  isGlobal     Boolean  @default(false) // true = available to all shops
  shop         String?                  // null for global templates
  usageCount   Int      @default(0)
  createdAt    DateTime @default(now())
}
```

## Template Data Structure (JSON)

```typescript
// QuizTemplate.templateData must match this shape exactly
interface TemplateData {
  type: string;  // "product-recommendation" | "personality" | "assessment" | "survey"
  settings: Record<string, unknown>;
  styling: Record<string, unknown>;
  questions: Array<{
    type: string;  // question type
    title: string;
    description?: string;
    required: boolean;
    position: number;
    settings: Record<string, unknown>;
    answers: Array<{
      text: string;
      position: number;
      score: number;
      productTags: string[];  // array of Shopify product tags
    }>;
  }>;
  resultPages: Array<{
    title: string;
    description?: string;
    type: string;  // "default" | "score-range" | "tag-match"
    minScore?: number;
    maxScore?: number;
    matchTags: string[];
    productLimit: number;
    layout: string;  // "grid" | "list" | "carousel"
    ctaText?: string;
    position: number;
  }>;
}
```

## Template Design Guidelines

### Question Design
- **5-10 questions** per template (sweet spot for engagement)
- Start broad → get specific progressively
- Mix question types: image-choice (visual preference) + multiple-choice (habits) + slider (intensity/budget)
- Each question must contribute to scoring/tagging
- Keep question text conversational: "What's your biggest skin concern?" not "Select skin concern:"
- Answers must include `productTags` arrays for recommendation matching

### Result Page Design
- **3-5 distinct profiles** per template
- Use descriptive titles: "The Minimalist", "Dry Skin Care Routine", "Performance Athlete"
- Include 2-3 sentence description explaining the recommendation
- Set `productLimit: 4` for grid layout, `productLimit: 3` for carousel
- Use score-range OR tag-match (not both in same template)

## Template Categories Reference

| Category     | Questions | Profiles | Primary Question Types           |
|--------------|-----------|----------|----------------------------------|
| Skincare     | 7-8       | 4-5      | image-choice, multiple-choice    |
| Fashion      | 6-8       | 4-5      | image-choice, multiple-choice    |
| Food         | 5-7       | 3-4      | multiple-choice, slider          |
| Fitness      | 6-8       | 3-4      | multiple-choice, rating          |
| Gift finder  | 5-6       | 4-5      | multiple-choice, slider          |
| Home decor   | 6-7       | 3-4      | image-choice, multiple-choice    |
| Pet products | 5-6       | 3-4      | multiple-choice, image-choice    |
| General      | 5-7       | 3-5      | mixed                            |

## Implementation Steps

### Step 1: Design the Template

Parse $ARGUMENTS → identify category → define:
1. Customer problem being solved
2. 3-5 distinct outcome profiles with unique names
3. 5-10 questions that progressively narrow to profiles
4. Scoring/tagging strategy

### Step 2: Build Template Data JSON

```typescript
// app/services/template.server.ts

const skincareMoistTemplate: TemplateData = {
  type: "product-recommendation",
  settings: { requireEmail: false, showProgressBar: true, randomizeQuestions: false },
  styling: { primaryColor: "#4CAF50", fontFamily: "inherit" },
  questions: [
    {
      type: "image-choice",
      title: "What's your skin type?",
      required: true,
      position: 0,
      settings: {},
      answers: [
        { text: "Dry", position: 0, score: 10, productTags: ["dry-skin", "moisturizing"] },
        { text: "Oily", position: 1, score: 0, productTags: ["oily-skin", "oil-control"] },
        { text: "Combination", position: 2, score: 5, productTags: ["combination", "balancing"] },
        { text: "Sensitive", position: 3, score: 8, productTags: ["sensitive", "gentle"] },
      ],
    },
    // ... more questions
  ],
  resultPages: [
    {
      title: "Intense Hydration Routine",
      description: "Your skin craves deep moisture. We've selected rich, nourishing products to restore your skin's natural barrier.",
      type: "score-range",
      minScore: 20,
      maxScore: 100,
      matchTags: [],
      productLimit: 4,
      layout: "grid",
      ctaText: "Shop my routine",
      position: 0,
    },
    // ... more result pages
  ],
};
```

### Step 3: Install Template as Quiz (Transaction)

```typescript
// app/services/template.server.ts

export async function installTemplate(templateId: string, shop: string): Promise<string> {
  const template = await db.quizTemplate.findUnique({ where: { id: templateId } });
  if (!template) throw new Error("Template not found");

  const data = (() => {
    try { return JSON.parse(template.templateData) as TemplateData; }
    catch { throw new Error("Invalid template data"); }
  })();

  const slug = await generateUniqueSlug(template.name, shop);

  const quiz = await db.$transaction(async (tx) => {
    const newQuiz = await tx.quiz.create({
      data: {
        shop,
        title: template.name,
        slug,
        status: "draft",
        type: data.type,
        settings: JSON.stringify(data.settings),
        styling: JSON.stringify(data.styling),
      },
    });

    for (const q of data.questions) {
      const question = await tx.question.create({
        data: {
          quizId: newQuiz.id,
          type: q.type,
          title: q.title,
          description: q.description,
          required: q.required,
          position: q.position,
          settings: JSON.stringify(q.settings),
        },
      });

      for (const a of q.answers) {
        await tx.answer.create({
          data: {
            questionId: question.id,
            text: a.text,
            position: a.position,
            score: a.score,
            productTags: JSON.stringify(a.productTags),
          },
        });
      }
    }

    for (const rp of data.resultPages) {
      await tx.resultPage.create({
        data: {
          quizId: newQuiz.id,
          title: rp.title,
          description: rp.description,
          type: rp.type,
          minScore: rp.minScore,
          maxScore: rp.maxScore,
          matchTags: JSON.stringify(rp.matchTags),
          productLimit: rp.productLimit,
          layout: rp.layout,
          ctaText: rp.ctaText,
          position: rp.position,
        },
      });
    }

    // Increment usage count
    await tx.quizTemplate.update({
      where: { id: templateId },
      data: { usageCount: { increment: 1 } },
    });

    return newQuiz;
  });

  return quiz.id;
}
```

### Step 4: Template Gallery UI (Polaris v13)

```tsx
// app/routes/app.templates.tsx
import { useLoaderData, useNavigation, useSubmit } from "react-router";  // NOT @remix-run/react
import { Page, Layout, Card, Grid, BlockStack, InlineStack, Text,
         Badge, Button, Thumbnail, EmptyState, Filters, ChoiceList } from "@shopify/polaris";

// Category filter
const CATEGORIES = [
  { label: "All", value: "" },
  { label: "Skincare", value: "skincare" },
  { label: "Fashion", value: "fashion" },
  { label: "Food", value: "food" },
  { label: "Fitness", value: "fitness" },
  { label: "Gift Finder", value: "general" },
];

// Template card:
<Grid.Cell columnSpan={{ xs: 6, sm: 4, md: 4, lg: 4 }}>
  <Card>
    <BlockStack gap="300">
      {template.thumbnail && (
        <Thumbnail source={template.thumbnail} alt={template.name} size="large" />
      )}
      <BlockStack gap="200">
        <InlineStack align="space-between">
          <Text variant="headingSm" as="h3">{template.name}</Text>
          {template.isGlobal && <Badge tone="info">Global</Badge>}
        </InlineStack>
        <Text as="p" tone="subdued">{template.description}</Text>
        <Text as="p" variant="bodySm" tone="subdued">
          {template.usageCount.toLocaleString()} installs
        </Text>
      </BlockStack>
      <Button
        variant="primary"
        fullWidth
        onClick={() => submit({ intent: "install", templateId: template.id }, { method: "POST" })}
        loading={navigation.state !== "idle"}
      >
        Use template
      </Button>
    </BlockStack>
  </Card>
</Grid.Cell>
```

## Quality Gate

- [ ] Template data matches TemplateData interface exactly
- [ ] `installTemplate` uses `$transaction` for atomicity
- [ ] All `JSON.parse` calls wrapped in try/catch (Law 6)
- [ ] Installed quiz is always `status: "draft"` (merchant publishes manually)
- [ ] Unique slug generated per shop after install
- [ ] `usageCount` incremented on install
- [ ] `npm run typecheck` — 0 errors

